#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:1
msgid "`@rescript-tauri/plugin-os`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:3
#, python-format
msgid ""
"ReScript bindings for the [Tauri 2.x OS info "
"plugin](https://v2.tauri.app/plugin/os-info/) — synchronous getters for "
"`platform` / `version` / `arch` / `family` and async getters for `locale`"
" / `hostname`. The 100% stable public surface of `@tauri-apps/plugin-os` "
"v2.3.x is covered, surfaced through four polymorphic-variant types that "
"mirror the upstream string-literal unions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:12
msgid ""
"The Phase 2 implementation is feature-complete in `main`. The first npm "
"publish (`plugin-os-v0.1.0`) is scheduled alongside the other Phase 2 "
"packages. Until then, consume `@rescript-tauri/plugin-os` via the source "
"repository or a workspace link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:19
msgid "Install"
msgstr "インストール"

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:25
msgid ""
"`@rescript-tauri/plugin-os` declares both `@rescript-tauri/core` and "
"`@tauri-apps/plugin-os` as `peerDependencies`, so you control each "
"upstream version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:29
msgid "Add the package to `dependencies` in your `rescript.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:40
msgid "On the Rust side, register the plugin on the builder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:58
msgid ""
"`tauri_plugin_os::init()` takes no configuration — the default builder is"
" sufficient for every API exposed by this binding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:61
msgid "Capabilities"
msgstr "Capability 設定"

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:75
msgid ""
"`os:default` grants the IPC permissions `allow-locale` and `allow-"
"hostname` that the two async getters require. The seven synchronous "
"getters do **not** travel over IPC (see [Sync getters](#sync-getters) "
"below) and therefore do not consume a capability — but the plugin must "
"still be registered on the Rust builder for the JavaScript globals to be "
"initialized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:82
msgid "Sync getters"
msgstr "Sync ゲッター"

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:84
msgid ""
"Seven of the nine functions resolve at call-site without ever touching "
"IPC: upstream caches the values on the "
"`window.__TAURI_OS_PLUGIN_INTERNALS__` global during plugin "
"initialization and the binding just reads them back. This makes them "
"cheap to call repeatedly, but it also means "
"`RescriptTauriCore.Mocks.mockIPC` **cannot intercept them** — runtime "
"tests stub `globalThis.window.__TAURI_OS_PLUGIN_INTERNALS__` directly "
"(see `packages/plugin-os/tests/runtime/plugin_os.test.mjs`)."
msgstr ""

