"Upstream JavaScript exposes the OS type through a function called `type`."
" `type` is reserved in ReScript, so the binding renames it to `osType_()`"
" (suffixed underscore matches the project-wide convention for reserved-"
"word avoidance):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:214
msgid "Sync getters don't go through IPC"
msgstr "Sync ゲッターは IPC を通らない"

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:216
msgid ""
"`Mocks.mockIPC` only intercepts IPC commands. The seven sync getters "
"bypass IPC entirely, so tests that need to fake their return values stub "
"the underlying global directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:234
msgid ""
"The async `locale()` / `hostname()` calls do go through IPC and can be "
"mocked with `Mocks.mockIPC` as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:237
msgid "`#x86_64`, `#powerpc64`, etc. are valid as-is"
msgstr "`#x86_64`、`#powerpc64` 等はそのまま使える"

#: ../../user/plugin-os.md:239
msgid ""
"ReScript polymorphic-variant tags accept `_` and digits, so the upstream "
"`\"x86_64\"` / `\"powerpc64\"` / `\"riscv64\"` / `\"s390x\"` / "
"`\"sparc64\"` strings translate to `#x86_64` / `#powerpc64` / `#riscv64` "
"/ `#s390x` / `#sparc64` without any quoting or escape."
msgstr ""

